    "v8": "Target node: CWD-1029 指针偏移量超出范围\n\nDefinition: a pointer is moved away from its base by offset/index/stride, and the code uses that new location without visible proof it is still inside the pointed span.\n\nTreat these as VULNERABLE:\n- `*(p + i)`, `p[i]`, `buf + off`, `(obj + 1)`, `cursor = cursor + sizeof(T)`, `temp + computed_len`, `virtBase + dataLen`\n- helper or safe-wrapper calls whose source or destination expression is already offset, such as `str + index`, `src + off`, `dst + 15`, or BY2W/parser helpers on a shifted pointer\n- loop or packet parsing code where the cursor/offset comes from external length, loop count, packet field, or computed size and no visible span proof covers the resulting address\n- guards that do not stop execution before the later offset use\n\nTreat these as BENIGN / not this node:\n- only the size argument or capacity metadata is wrong on the original pointer\n- fixed local array/member indexing overflow\n- null pointer / uninitialized pointer state\n- explicit total-length proof that covers the later indexed trailing-array access\n\nChoose CWD-1029 only when the out-of-range derived pointer location is the core bug.\nIf uncertain, output BENIGN.\nReturn exactly one token: VULNERABLE or BENIGN."
